<title>ITALY: Italian mini-budget to be ready by March 30 - Prodi.</title>
<headline>Italian mini-budget to be ready by March 30 - Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The mini-budget being prepared by the Italian government will be ready by Easter, Prime Minister Romano Prodi told a news conference.</p>
<p>Asked if the budget would be presented this Thursday, Prodi replied: &quot;I can confirm that the budget will be done before Easter&quot;. Easter Sunday is on March 30.</p>
<p>Political sources said the package, which is expected to include up to 16 trillion lire of deficit-cutting measures, should be approved by the cabinet on Thursday or Friday.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
